{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":126252,"duration_api_ms":270983,"num_turns":6,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"48136683-b452-43d6-b71d-4c5916ae0a2c","total_cost_usd":0.8240132999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":1718,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28670,"cache_read_input_tokens":80301,"output_tokens":2306,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28670,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1061,"outputTokens":19170,"cacheReadInputTokens":2378293,"cacheCreationInputTokens":162956,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5384352999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1718,"outputTokens":2306,"cacheReadInputTokens":80301,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28670,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.285578,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All four amendments address real, verified issues. Three target correctness or regression coverage gaps (calibration invariant, E2E deserialization, stale cache inconsistency), and one addresses a confirmed triple-duplication of domain metadata across crates. Each is well-scoped and justified by code inspection.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-528ad2ff","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: REFERENCE_SA_V_CM2_PER_L = 1000.0/19.0 exactly matches the default TankState geometry (40x25 cm footprint, 22 L gross, 3 cm substrate → 19 L net). The constant is used in 5 call sites for gas exchange normalization via compute_o2_kla, where it controls the SA/V ratio scaling. No existing test validates this calibration link. If default dimensions, fill height, or substrate displacement change, the ratio silently drifts from 1.0, shifting all default-tank gas exchange. A single regression test is trivially cheap and guards a non-obvious invariant that would otherwise break silently."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-05a63920","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: normalize_snapshot_object backfills canonical chemistry keys from legacy aliases but does not strip the 3 API-injected metadata fields (chemistry_field_semantics, estimated_tds_scope, legacy_chemistry_aliases). Deserialization succeeds only because TankSnapshot lacks #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. Existing tests in api_client.rs cover legacy-only payloads but never exercise the full enriched response shape produced by snapshot_response_json(). An E2E deserialization test that round-trips through the actual server enrichment function would catch schema drift at the API/TUI integration boundary — a gap the current 6 tests across both modules do not cover."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-95eadc35","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed real consistency bug. TankSnapshot::from_state() freshly solves carbonate equilibrium from authoritative DIC + alkalinity (producing correct pH/CO2), but immediately reads TDS/conductivity through chemistry.tds_mg_per_l() → total_tracked_ions_mg() → bicarbonate_mg_total, which is explicitly documented as a stale-able cache. Plant growth, algae growth, and nitrification all mutate DIC or alkalinity without calling resolve_carbonate_state(), and the stale window spans up to 23 hours in the simulation cycle. This produces snapshots with internally inconsistent chemistry: fresh pH paired with stale bicarbonate-backed TDS. The fix — deriving bicarbonate from the fresh carbonate_eq.hco3_mmol_per_l or forcing a cache refresh — is straightforward and eliminates a real data integrity issue."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-0fe2ed5a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed triple duplication: the 7-ion set is defined as an explicit string array in tank_api (TRACKED_TDS_IONS), as a narrative in tank_tui (ESTIMATED_TDS_SCOPE_LINES), and implicitly in the code of tank_core's total_tracked_ions_mg(). The omitted-species list is duplicated between tank_api and tank_tui. If the ion set changes, 3+ files plus their tests must be updated in lockstep with no compile-time enforcement. Centralizing the authoritative ion-set and scope metadata in tank_core eliminates this drift risk. Both API and TUI can import and format the shared definition for their respective needs."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"cc100bf7-1261-42e2-96aa-6dad411ddb85"}
